Z||000008||80's BOY||09-07-2000||09:48 AM||||i made my own side scoop similar to the holley one, but better. it was a cheesy tape on scoop from jc whitney. i then cut about $15 worth of plastic off the damn thing, and molded it onto the side of the car. it turned out really smooth and looked like a pro job. makes a loud hiss when you get on it!!||||reg||1
Z||000009||Philphine||09-09-2000||11:08 PM||||i've got some extra panels and i'm always looking for vents that might work. there's a big swap meet here this weekend but i'm broke and i have guard any way.for the moment i have some scoops off a '69 (i think) mustang laying around and some camaro hood scoops similar to what some one else was thinking about molding on to their hood.<P>i want to try some thing cheap for my $300 (and rising) fiero. <P>forgot i just got this thing from work. it's an intake for a fan thing that sits on a 50 gal. drum. i like it but it sticks out too far. if i can work out how to section it (and get another for the other side. they may get more since they come with a particular motor but they don't use the vent) it might look and work pretty good.<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 09-09-2000).]||||reg||1
